.TH PHASORSTD_FILE 3 "July 2026" "Phasor 4.0.0" "Phasor Standard Library 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
phasorstd_file \- Phasor file system functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B include "std/file.phs";
.PP
.B fopen(path, mode)
.B fclose(fd)
.B fabsolute(path)
.B fstem(path)
.B fname(path)
.B fext(path)
.B fparent(path)
.B fjoin(path1, path2)
.B fisdir(path)
.B fread(path_or_fd)
.B fwrite(path_or_fd, content)
.B fexists(path)
.B freadln(path_or_fd[, line_number])
.B fwriteln(path, line_number, content)
.B fappend(path_or_fd, content)
.B frm(path)
.B frn(old_path, new_path)
.B fcd([path])
.B fcp(source, dest[, overwrite])
.B fmv(source, dest)
.B fpropset(path, property, value)
.B fpropget(path, property)
.B fmk(path)
.B fmkdir(path)
.B frmdir(path, recurse)
.B freaddir(path)
.B fsize(path)
.B fcp_progress(files, dest)
.fi
.SH FILE DESCRIPTORS
.TP
.BR fopen (path, mode)
Open a file and return a reusable file descriptor. This is the only way to obtain a descriptor
that can be passed to \fBfread()\fR, \fBfwrite()\fR, \fBfreadln()\fR, and \fBfappend()\fR instead of a path.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file to open
.IP \fBmode\fR 12
Mode string. Recognized modes: \fB"r"\fR (read), \fB"w"\fR (write, truncating), \fB"a"\fR (append),
\fB"r+"\fR (read/write, no truncation), \fB"w+"\fR (read/write, truncating), \fB"a+"\fR (read/append).
Any other combination of the characters \fBr\fR, \fBw\fR, \fBa\fR, and \fB+\fR is also accepted and
interpreted using the same rules.
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Integer file descriptor on success, or null if the file could not be opened
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fclose (fd)
Close a file descriptor previously returned by \fBfopen()\fR.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBfd\fR 12
Integer file descriptor
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if the descriptor was valid and closed, false otherwise
.RE
.SH PATH UTILITIES
.TP
.BR fabsolute (path)
Get the absolute path of a file.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Absolute (weakly canonical) path string
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fstem (path)
Get the stem (filename without extension) of a path.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the stem component. For example, given \fB"archive.tar.gz"\fR, returns \fB"archive.tar"\fR.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fname (path)
Get the filename component of a path, including its extension.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the filename. For example, given \fB"/home/user/docs/report.txt"\fR, returns \fB"report.txt"\fR.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fext (path)
Get the file extension of a path.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the extension, including the leading dot. For example, given \fB"report.txt"\fR, returns \fB".txt"\fR. Returns an empty string if there is no extension.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fparent (path)
Get the parent directory of a path.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file or directory
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the parent path. For example, given \fB"/home/user/docs/report.txt"\fR, returns \fB"/home/user/docs"\fR.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fjoin (path1, path2)
Join two path components together.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath1\fR 12
The base path
.IP \fBpath2\fR 12
The path to append
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the joined path, using the platform's native path separator.
.RE
.SH FILE I/O FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR fread (path_or_fd)
Read the entire contents of a file, either by path or from an open file descriptor.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath_or_fd\fR 12
File path, or an integer file descriptor returned by \fBfopen()\fR. When a descriptor is given,
the remaining unread contents of the stream are read from its current position.
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the file (or remaining stream) contents, or null if the path cannot be opened
or the descriptor is invalid
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fwrite (path_or_fd, content)
Write content to a file, overwriting existing content, or write to an open file descriptor.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath_or_fd\fR 12
File path (opened fresh and truncated), or an integer file descriptor from \fBfopen()\fR
(written at its current position)
.IP \fBcontent\fR 12
String to write
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success, false if the descriptor is invalid
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if a path (not a descriptor) cannot be opened
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fappend (path_or_fd, content)
Append content to the end of a file, or to an open file descriptor.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath_or_fd\fR 12
File path, or an integer file descriptor from \fBfopen()\fR. When a descriptor is given, the
write position is moved to the end of the stream before appending.
.IP \fBcontent\fR 12
String to append
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success, false if the descriptor is invalid
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if a path (not a descriptor) cannot be opened
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR freadln (path_or_fd[, line_number])
Read a line from a file, either sequentially from an open descriptor or by line index.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath_or_fd\fR 12
File path, or an integer file descriptor from \fBfopen()\fR
.IP \fBline_number\fR 12
Zero-based line index. Optional, but only when \fBpath_or_fd\fR is a file descriptor.
.RE
.PP
.B Description:
Two calling conventions are supported. Called with a single file descriptor argument,
.B freadln()
reads the next line sequentially from the descriptor's current position (useful for looping
over a file line by line). Called with a \fBline_number\fR, it seeks a descriptor back to the
start of the stream (or opens \fBpath_or_fd\fR fresh if it is a path) and reads forward to the
requested line.
.PP
.B Returns:
String containing the line content without its trailing newline; null if the file descriptor
is invalid or already at end of stream; empty string if \fBline_number\fR is beyond the last
line in the file
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if called with zero arguments or more than two; if called with a single argument
that is not a file descriptor (a bare path with no \fBline_number\fR is not valid); or if a path
(not a descriptor) cannot be opened for the two-argument form
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fwriteln (path, line_number, content)
Write content to a specific line in a file, expanding the file with empty lines if necessary.
Unlike \fBfread()\fR, \fBfwrite()\fR, \fBfreadln()\fR, and \fBfappend()\fR, this function only
accepts a file path; it does not accept a file descriptor.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file (must be a path, not a file descriptor)
.IP \fBline_number\fR 12
Zero-based line index
.IP \fBcontent\fR 12
New line content
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBpath\fR is a file descriptor instead of a path, or if the file cannot be
opened for reading or writing
.RE
.SH FILE OPERATIONS
.TP
.BR fexists (path)
Check if a file or directory exists.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file or directory
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if path exists, false otherwise
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fisdir (path)
Check if a path refers to a directory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to check
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if the path exists and is a directory, false otherwise
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fmk (path)
Create a new empty file.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file to create
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if file cannot be created
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR frm (path)
Remove (delete) a file.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file to delete
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if file was deleted, false if file didn't exist
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR frn (old_path, new_path)
Rename a file.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBold_path\fR 12
Current file path
.IP \fBnew_path\fR 12
New file path
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if renamed, false if source didn't exist
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fcp (source, dest[, overwrite])
Copy a file.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBsource\fR 12
Source file path
.IP \fBdest\fR 12
Destination file path
.IP \fBoverwrite\fR 12
Boolean to allow overwriting (optional, default false)
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success, false on failure
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fmv (source, dest)
Move a file (copy then delete source).
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBsource\fR 12
Source file path
.IP \fBdest\fR 12
Destination file path
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true only if both the copy and the subsequent removal of \fBsource\fR succeed. Returns
false if the copy step fails (\fBdest\fR is left untouched), or if the copy succeeds but
\fBsource\fR could not be removed afterward (in which case both files remain on disk).
.RE
.SH DIRECTORY OPERATIONS
.TP
.BR fcd ([path])
Get or set the current working directory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
New working directory (optional)
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Current working directory path. If path argument provided, changes to that directory first
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fmkdir (path)
Create a new directory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path of the directory to create
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if created, false if directory already exists
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR frmdir (path, recurse)
Remove a directory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Directory path
.IP \fBrecurse\fR 12
Boolean; if true, removes the directory and all of its contents. If false, removes the
directory only if it is empty. This argument is required, not optional.
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if the directory (and, when \fBrecurse\fR is true, its contents) was removed, or
if \fBpath\fR did not exist to begin with. Returns false if \fBrecurse\fR is false and the
directory is not empty, or if a recursive removal fails partway through.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR freaddir (path)
List contents of a directory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the directory to list
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Array of strings, one per entry in the directory (filenames only, not full paths; both files
and subdirectories are included)
.PP
.B Throws:
An underlying filesystem error if \fBpath\fR does not exist or is not a directory
.RE
.SH FILE METADATA
.TP
.BR fsize (path)
Get the size of a file in bytes.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
Path to the file
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Integer file size in bytes
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fpropset (path, property, value)
Set a file property (timestamp).
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
File path
.IP \fBproperty\fR 12
Property character ('a'=access, 'm'=modify)
.IP \fBvalue\fR 12
Unix timestamp (epoch seconds)
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true on success, false on failure
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBvalue\fR is a negative integer
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR fpropget (path, property)
Get a file property (timestamp).
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBpath\fR 12
File path
.IP \fBproperty\fR 12
Property character ('a'=access, 'm'=modify)
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Integer Unix timestamp (epoch seconds). This function always returns an integer; it does not
return null. Consult the runtime's platform-specific behavior for the sentinel value used on
failure (e.g.\& a negative number)
.RE
.SH PHASOR-LEVEL HELPERS
.TP
.BR fcp_progress (files, dest)
Copy a list of files into a destination directory, printing a progress bar to the console as
each file completes. This is a Phasor-level convenience function defined in \fBphs/file.phs\fR
itself (built on top of \fBfcp()\fR, \fBfjoin()\fR, and \fBfname()\fR); it is not a native
function, and is only available once \fBphs/file.phs\fR has been included, since it also pulls
in the progress-bar extra.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBfiles\fR 12
Array of source file paths
.IP \fBdest\fR 12
Destination directory path
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Boolean true if every file copied successfully, false as soon as any single copy fails (the
function stops at the first failure and does not attempt the remaining files)
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Basic File I/O
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/file.phs";

// Write to file
fwrite("data.txt", "Hello, World!");

// Read from file
var content = fread("data.txt");
puts(content);

// Append to file
fappend("data.txt", "\nNew line");
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B File Descriptors
.PP
.nf
.RS
// Open once, read/write multiple times without reopening the path
var fd = fopen("data.txt", "r+");
if (fd != null) {
    var line = freadln(fd);       // read the next line sequentially
    fappend(fd, "\nAppended via fd");
    fclose(fd);
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Line-Based Operations
.PP
.nf
.RS
// Read a specific line by index
var line = freadln("config.txt", 0);

// Update a specific line (path only; fwriteln does not accept a descriptor)
fwriteln("config.txt", 2, "new_setting=value");
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Path Utilities
.PP
.nf
.RS
var p = "/home/user/docs/report.txt";

puts(fname(p));    // "report.txt"
puts(fstem(p));    // "report"
puts(fext(p));     // ".txt"
puts(fparent(p));  // "/home/user/docs"

var full = fjoin("/home/user", "docs/report.txt");
puts(fabsolute("../project"));

// Check before operating
if (fisdir("/home/user/docs")) {
    var entries = freaddir("/home/user/docs");
    for (var i: i64 = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
        puts(entries[i]);
    }
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B File Management
.PP
.nf
.RS
// Check existence
if (fexists("old.txt")) {
    // Rename file
    frn("old.txt", "new.txt");
}

// Copy with overwrite
fcp("source.txt", "backup.txt", true);

// Move file
fmv("temp.txt", "archive/temp.txt");

// Delete file
frm("unwanted.txt");
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Directory Operations
.PP
.nf
.RS
// Get current directory
var cwd = fcd();
puts(cwd);

// Change directory
fcd("/home/user/projects");

// Create directory
fmkdir("new_folder");

// List directory (returns an array of filenames)
var entries = freaddir(".");
for (var i: i64 = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
    puts(entries[i]);
}

// Remove directory recursively (recurse argument is required)
frmdir("old_folder", true);
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B File Size
.PP
.nf
.RS
var bytes = fsize("document.txt");
putf("Size: %d bytes\n", bytes);
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B File Properties
.PP
.nf
.RS
// Get modification time
var mtime = fpropget("file.txt", 'm');
puts(mtime);

// Set access time
var now = time();
fpropset("file.txt", 'a', now);
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Copying Files With a Progress Bar
.PP
.nf
.RS
var files = ["a.txt", "b.txt", "c.txt"];
var ok = fcp_progress(files, "/backup/destination");
if (!ok) {
    puts("One or more files failed to copy");
}
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
File paths can be relative or absolute
.IP \(bu 2
.B fread()\fR,\fB fwrite()\fR,\fB freadln()\fR,\fB and fappend()
accept either a path string or an integer file descriptor from \fBfopen()\fR as their first
argument; \fBfwriteln()\fR only accepts a path
.IP \(bu 2
Line numbers in
.B freadln()
and
.B fwriteln()
are zero-based
.IP \(bu 2
.B fwriteln()
expands the file with empty lines if necessary
.IP \(bu 2
.B fmv()
is implemented as copy + delete, not an atomic move
.IP \(bu 2
.B frmdir()
requires its \fBrecurse\fR argument; it is not optional, and removal only affects an empty
directory unless \fBrecurse\fR is true
.IP \(bu 2
Property characters: 'a' for access time, 'm' for modification time
.IP \(bu 2
.B fstem()
strips only the last extension; \fB"archive.tar.gz"\fR yields \fB"archive.tar"\fR
.IP \(bu 2
.B fext()
returns an empty string if the path has no extension
